WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.120
We now have new allegations against beleaguered&nbsp;
Republican Congressman Matt Gates. We've already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:13.680
discussed his alleged involvement in child sex&nbsp;
trafficking and or possibly paying minors for sex.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.000
There is a whole world of scandal for Matt Gates&nbsp;
related to that. But now there's a totally new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.680
problem for him. He is suspected of being&nbsp;
involved in a shill candidate scheme. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.360
a shill candidate scheme or a ghost candidate&nbsp;
scheme is one where if I'm running or if my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:38.480
friend is running, I might induce or help someone&nbsp;
else run, not because I want them to win, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:44.240
because I want them to siphon off votes from my&nbsp;
opponent. And I'll explain exactly how it worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:50.640
in this case. In Florida's thirty seventh and&nbsp;
thirty ninth districts, Alex Rodriguez and Celso&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:57.920
Alfonso ran for office. One of the candidates has&nbsp;
already been charged. The believed mastermind is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:04.080
guy called Frank R. Tilles, a resigned Florida&nbsp;
senator. And now we've learned of a third Schill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:10.240
candidate named Justin Ayanami, who ran in the 9th&nbsp;
District in Florida. All three of these candidates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:16.480
appear to be funded by the same dark money through&nbsp;
a PAC called our Florida PAC and a PAC called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:23.520
The Truth PAC for Central Florida. Both PACs are&nbsp;
funded by a single, untraceable Atlanta company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.880
called Proclivity that made only one expenditure&nbsp;
to a printing company called Advance Impression.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.080
It's all weird. And the Matt Gates piece is that&nbsp;
Gates appears to be connected to that central&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:42.320
Florida aspect of this. And the idea is that&nbsp;
Justin Jannati ran as an independent to help the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:49.360
Republican Jason Obrador win by taking votes away&nbsp;
as a left leaning independent from the Democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:56.000
candidate, Patricia Sigmon. Every aspect of this&nbsp;
is imploding. Florida lobbyist Chris Dorward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.040
who is the person that talked to Matt Gates&nbsp;
about the Schill candidate, Justin Einaudi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.440
resigned on Friday from his lobbying&nbsp;
firm. Now, it's important to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.840
it doesn't appear that the being involved&nbsp;
with creating a shill candidate is illegal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.800
The criminal part and we're still learning&nbsp;
this is my best reading as of right now. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.160
criminal part would be the dark money funding all&nbsp;
of this. And it's basically just a spoiler scheme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.400
that appears to be legal as long as it's funded&nbsp;
legally and transparently. And the idea is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.960
if I'm a Republican and I'm running against the&nbsp;
Democrat and it's expected to be tight 50/50,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:39.120
it could come down to a half point. I go out&nbsp;
and recruit a left leaning independent to run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.880
so that they will siphon votes away from my&nbsp;
opponent and I as the Republican win. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.680
the strategy. In a sense. This is what Trump was&nbsp;
doing with the reports that people around Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:56.240
were advising and encouraging Kanye West to run.&nbsp;
The belief being if Kanye runs, it'll take votes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:01.600
away from Joe Biden and it'll be good for Donald&nbsp;
Trump. It's a slimy practice. It's not a new one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:07.360
It appears to be legal as long as you do it in the&nbsp;
particular way where the funding is transparent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:12.240
Democrats could do this. Democrats could do this&nbsp;
by starting to register and help libertarian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.440
candidates run across the country. You might&nbsp;
have a tight Senate race, could be 51 49 for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:24.480
Republican. You bring in some freedom, free market&nbsp;
libertarian, and then if they take three points&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:30.960
from your opponent, you win. That's the idea. Will&nbsp;
Matt Gates ultimately get arrested for something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:36.000
or is he going to escape scot free for everything&nbsp;
he is suspected of? Let me know your thoughts.

